{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerUnitCircle","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerUnitCircle","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_unit_circle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_unit_circle","kind":"opaque","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerUnitCircle.lean#L55-L67","doc":"The Bloch-Wigner dilogarithm on the unit circle:\n`D(e^{iθ}) = Cl_2 θ`, where `Cl_2` is the Clausen function.\n\nDeclared as `noncomputable opaque` rather than `axiom`: the\nfunction exists with this signature, but its body is sealed\npending the canonical Clausen-function integration (Phase 3\nresearch-grade closure).  Downstream consumers depend only on\nthe signature.\n\nSee the sibling filler at\n`folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-wigner-mathlib-filler.lean`\nfor the candidate body `Cl_2 θ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}